## inspiration 

this app is not necessarily solving a problem, but a creating a convenience. i recently took a course on coffee: biology, culture, and trade. i was fascinated by consumer discovery that emphasized coffee shops as an extension of social (and sometimes political values).
social media apps offer brands a marketing avenue, but the apps are increasingly satured and not location-specific (unless explicitly prompted). 
consumers should drive sentiment and quality, not the marketing budget behind the business; hierarchy should not be determined by $ spent, but consumer utility provided.
----- also i am a huge fan of Beli. I have visited many coffee shops, across various locations, and would love a record of which drinks and places i love (with picutres alongside it).
if you want to filter based on productivity-level (social - locked in, will add in later based on consumer feedback). that can also be a feature. if you want to invite your friends or meet a mentor, you can send the invitation through our app (maybe later on). 
there will also be a profile component, yes where you can see places you have been and want to try, but also where you can set your current favorite drink 
